    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="7" relname="preparation">I can identify with your comments P52.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="8" relname="circumstance">As I learn more about objectoriented analysis and design(OOAD),</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="8" relname="span">I see how its very nature andbuilding blocks, the class, provide for better intuitiveness in thefinal product.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="5" relname="circumstance">For example, once an Employee class has been createdwith attributes such as  name, employeeID, pay rate,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="9" relname="span">any specializationsor subclasses that follow such as Project Manager, Systems Analyst, DBA,will automatically inherit the same attributes.</segment>
        <group id="6" type="span"/>
